# cut.env -- every input to an Ostler DMG cut, in ONE committed file.
# ============================================================================
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# Until v1.0.15 the cut was driven by env vars typed onto the `make ship`
# command line, remembered from chat scrollback or a defib note. That is how
# v1.0.14.1 was cut from a tree 161 commits behind origin/main and still passed
# 39 of 40 gates: nothing recorded which inputs the cut was supposed to use, so
# nothing could disagree with what it actually used.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the NEXT cut. It is committed, so
# `git log cut.env` is the history of what every cut shipped.
#
#   Usage:   make -C gui cut          # sources this file, runs the ship chain
#   Or:      set -a; . ./cut.env; set +a; make -C gui ship
#
# NO ABSOLUTE OPERATOR PATHS. Everything hangs off $HOME or the repo root, so
# this file stays clean for the PII scanner and works on any cut machine.
# Per-machine overrides belong in the environment, never edited in here.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. WHAT THIS CUT IS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The installer version is NOT set here -- it lives in gui/project.yml +
# gui/OstlerInstaller/Info.plist + the generated pbxproj, and
# tests/test_installer_version_consistency.sh enforces all three agree.
# Bumping it ALSO requires cut-manifests/v<major.minor.patch>.yaml to exist,
# or the per-cut half of the manifest gate silently selects nothing.
CUT_VERSION=1.0.15
CUT_DATE=2026-08-06

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. THE HUB (Tauri Ostler.app)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built by `cargo tauri build` from apps/ in the ostler-assistant checkout that
# matches DAEMON_COMMIT below. verify-commit-parity fails the cut if the Hub
# wrapper and the daemon embed different web/dist commits, so these two MUST be
# built from the same tree.
#
# TRAP: `cargo tauri build` only WARNS when APPLE_ID is unset -- it produces an
# un-notarised bundle and exits 0. That no longer matters for stapling (the cut
# notarises the Hub itself, see #221 below) but it does mean you cannot infer
# "notarised" from a green build.
OSTLER_APP_PATH="${HOME}/Developer/oa-reconcile-452/target/release/bundle/macos/Ostler.app"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. THE DAEMON (ostler-assistant)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DAEMON_VERSION + DAEMON_SHA256 live in gui/Makefile and install.sh -- FOUR
# pin sites in total, and sites 2 and 4 are the ones nothing used to compare:
#   gui/Makefile   DAEMON_VERSION, DAEMON_SHA256
#   install.sh     OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION, DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256
# v1.0.15 pin: 0.4.53 / sha256 2363d977...  (tag hub-v0.4.53 = ff57be3f)
#
# OSTLER_ASSISTANT_DIR must be a real CLONE checked out AT THE TAG -- the gates
# read its HEAD, and one of them tests `-d .git`, so a git worktree fails.
OSTLER_ASSISTANT_DIR="${HOME}/Developer/ostler-assistant"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. SOURCE CHECKOUTS THE GATES READ
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are read-only to the cut: the manifest + provenance gates grep them at
# pinned SHAs to prove a merged fix is really in the artefact.
CM044_DIR="${HOME}/Documents/Projects/CM044 - PWG Personal Wiki"
HR015_DIR="${HOME}/Documents/Projects/HR015 - Gaming PC"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. NOTARISATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `xcrun notarytool store-credentials <alias>` must already hold this profile.
# The cut submits THREE times: nested Ostler.app, the outer installer .app, and
# the DMG wrapper.
NOTARY_PROFILE=ostler-installer

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. WIKI IMAGES -- READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING A DIGEST
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins live in install.sh, NOT here (install.sh is what ships). Recorded for
# provenance:
#   ghcr.io/creativemachines-ai/ostler-wiki-site@sha256:f2acc0df...
#   ghcr.io/creativemachines-ai/ostler-wiki-compiler@sha256:2b7d494e...
#   both built from CM044 tag v0.1.2 = cd79c502 = CM044 origin/main tip
#
# ghcr.io/creativemachines-ai is the LIVE publish target: CM044's
# .github/workflows/release-images.yml builds on a `v*` TAG PUSH and pushes
# there with the CM_AI_GHCR_PAT classic PAT (renewed 2026-08-02, expires
# 2027-08-02). ghcr.io/ostler-ai is the DEPRECATED pre-#31 namespace -- images
# STILL RESOLVE there, so a pin against it pulls happily while carrying
# whatever was last hand-pushed, with no CI provenance behind it.
#
# This has now been got backwards TWICE (2026-08-02 and 2026-08-06), both times
# by reading release state off a local checkout instead of CM051 origin/main.
# On 2026-08-06 it shipped a wiki image built from an unmerged CM044 branch four
# commits behind main, missing the customer-visible iframe-chrome fix d0eea98.
# Three gates were then widened to accept it. All reverted; test case (m) in
# tests/test_cut_freshness_gate.sh now proves an ostler-ai pin goes RED.
#
# NOT A CONTRADICTION: install.sh also pins ghcr.io/ostler-ai/vane and
# ghcr.io/oxigraph/oxigraph. Those are mirrored THIRD-PARTY images, nothing to
# do with the wiki namespace policy. The gate only polices ostler-wiki-*.
#
# TO SHIP A NEWER WIKI (e.g. the reskin): merge to CM044 main -> push a v0.1.x
# tag -> let release-images.yml publish -> re-pin install.sh to the new
# creativemachines-ai digests -> update scripts/wiki_image_provenance.tsv.
# Do NOT hand-build. Do NOT push to ostler-ai.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. GATE COMPARISON BASES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both default to `main` inside the gates; set here so the cut record is
# explicit about what "fresh" was measured against.
#
# DAEMON_INTEGRATION_BRANCH was `integration/hub-v1.0.9` until 2026-08-06. That
# branch is DEAD -- 36 commits behind ostler-assistant main while carrying 78
# main lacks -- so a daemon built from trunk could never satisfy it.
DAEMON_INTEGRATION_BRANCH=main
CM044_BRANCH=main

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. BUILD SCRATCH (outside iCloud on purpose)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iCloud's FileProvider tags freshly-built files with com.apple.FinderInfo
# AFTER the in-build xattr strip, which makes codesign reject the bundle with
# "resource fork, Finder information, or similar detritus not allowed".
# Defaults in gui/Makefile already point at /tmp; listed for completeness.
# BUILD_DIR=/tmp/ostler-installer-build-${USER}
# DIST_DIR=/tmp/ostler-installer-dist-${USER}
